[center][size=6][b]KOTOR Co-op[/b][/size]
[size=4]Seamless drop-in, drop-out co-op for Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic[/size][/center]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/main/nexus/images/1-cover-title.jpg[/img][/center]

[b][color=#ff9900]EXPERIMENTAL BETA.[/color][/b] Read [b]What to expect[/b] below before you install. Back up your saves first.

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]
Two to eight people each run their own copy of KOTOR 1 and play in one shared world, each as their own character. It is modelled on the Elden Ring "seamless co-op" style of mod: nobody sets up a server, and there is no lobby to leave the game for. You start the game, press [b]Co-op[/b] on the main menu, and host or connect. Players can drop in and out.

[list]
[*]See each other as real in-game characters, walk through the same doors and fly to the same planets
[*]Fight the same enemies (they scale up with more players) and watch the same conversations
[*]Your own backpack and credits; quest items, doors, chests, the journal and merchant stock are shared
[*]Saving, loading, quitting to the menu and even the host crashing are handled; the other player rejoins on its own
[*]In-game console (~) and chat (Enter)
[*]Works with GOG and Steam copies, version 1.0.3. KOTOR 2 is not touched.
[/list]

